imgsensor: ov9734: apply the vertical flip Amazon intended

The OV9734 devices (crown, checkers) produce an upside-down picture. The
cause is not the mounting: it is a Kconfig symbol that is never set.

ov9734mipiraw_Sensor.h picks its MIRROR macro like this:

    #if defined(CONFIG_CAMERA_MULTIMODAL)
    #define ov9734_MIRROR_V
    #else
    #define ov9734_MIRROR_NORMAL
    #endif

CONFIG_CAMERA_MULTIMODAL is declared "default n" in
drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/Kconfig and is set by no Echo Show
defconfig, so the condition can never be true and every build gets
ov9734_MIRROR_NORMAL. MIRROR is 0x10 rather than 0x14, register 0x3820
never gets its flip bit, and the sensor reads out inverted.

The multimodal branch is the one meant for these devices, so this makes
the vertical flip unconditional rather than enabling the symbol. Turning
the symbol on would reach further than the picture: it also switches
SUPPORT_I2C_BUS_NUM2 from 2 to 0 and skips adopt_CAMERA_HW_CheckIsAlive()
in kd_sensorlist.c, neither of which is wanted here.

sensor_output_dataformat stays RAW_B. Amazon's own multimodal
configuration pairs MIRROR_V with RAW_B, and .mirror in this driver is
assigned once and never read again - unlike the OV02B10 in patches/0007,
which has a live set_mirror_flip(). The Bayer phase the HAL is told about
must therefore stay as it is; declaring RAW_R here swaps red and blue.

Verified on crown (Echo Show 8) and checkers (Echo Show 5 1st gen), each
by a community report with photos: upright picture with correct colour,
ro.camera.sensor_orientation left at 0.

This replaces an earlier version of this patch that selected
ov9734_MIRROR_HV and changed sensor_output_dataformat to RAW_R. That was
wrong twice over. It mirrored the horizontal axis as well, which Amazon
does not do and which leaves the image left-right reversed, and the
matching Bayer change was carried over from the OV02B10 where both axes
really do move. It looked upright because a horizontal mirror is easy to
miss on a front-facing camera; the red/blue swap it introduced is a large
part of the colour trouble reported on crown.

Both devices that share this driver are therefore confirmed; they mount
the sensor the same way.

Apply from the kernel tree (kernel/amazon/mt8163-4.9):
    patch -p1 < 0014-imgsensor-ov9734-vertical-flip.patch

--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/mt8163/ov9734_mipi_raw/ov9734mipiraw_Sensor.h
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/mt8163/ov9734_mipi_raw/ov9734mipiraw_Sensor.h
@@ -16,11 +16,16 @@
 #ifndef _OV9734MIPI_SENSOR_H
 #define _OV9734MIPI_SENSOR_H

-#if defined(CONFIG_CAMERA_MULTIMODAL)
+/*
+ * Unconditional on purpose. This used to be selected by
+ * CONFIG_CAMERA_MULTIMODAL, which is "default n" and set by no Echo Show
+ * defconfig, so the sensor always fell through to MIRROR_NORMAL and read
+ * out upside down. The multimodal branch is the one meant for these
+ * devices. Enabling the symbol instead would also change
+ * SUPPORT_I2C_BUS_NUM2 and skip the CheckIsAlive ioctl in
+ * kd_sensorlist.c, which is not wanted.
+ */
 #define ov9734_MIRROR_V
-#else
-#define ov9734_MIRROR_NORMAL
-#endif


 #if defined(ov9734_MIRROR_NORMAL)
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/mt8163/ov9734_mipi_raw/ov9734mipiraw_Sensor.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/mt8163/ov9734_mipi_raw/ov9734mipiraw_Sensor.c
@@ -155,7 +155,7 @@


 static imgsensor_struct imgsensor = {
-        .mirror = IMAGE_NORMAL,                                    /* mirrorflip information */
+        .mirror = IMAGE_V_MIRROR,                                  /* mirrorflip information */
         .sensor_mode = IMGSENSOR_MODE_INIT,                        /* IMGSENSOR_MODE enum value,record current sensor mode,such as: INIT, Preview, Capture, Video,High Speed Video, Slim Video */
         .shutter = 0x3D0,                                          /* current shutter */
         .gain = 0x100,                                             /* current gain */
